.TH buffer_putxlonglong0 3
.SH NAME
buffer_putxlonglong0 \- write a zero-padded hexadecimal 64-bit integer to a buffer
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <buffer.h>
.B #include <fmt.h>

int \fBbuffer_putxlonglong0\fP(buffer* \fIb\fP, uint64 \fIl\fP, int \fIpad\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbuffer_putxlonglong0\fP formats the 64-bit integer \fIl\fP as a hexadecimal
string and writes it to the buffer \fIb\fP. If the resulting string is shorter
than \fIpad\fP, the buffer is padded with leading '0' characters.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 on error (setting \fIerrno\fP).
.SH SEE ALSO
buffer_put(3), fmt_xlonglong(3), buffer_putxlonglong(3)